{"author":{"id":"8022379585b4ab99ca8775db3eb67d33fcb256817114c28e51ccc1e9f55cdec4"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1792310648,"nonce":"F7NPbel7RFtd7qu0nXhhEh8LDaE=","title":"2026-09-24 37927082..38aa4db7 (635-\u003e647) — \\\"close every macro gap\\\" round 1: macro catch semantics, runtime `macro e`, and the COMPILER ...","message":"User asked (2026-09-24) to \"close every macro gap\". Round 1 landed 37927082, 6b5fe751, 38aa4db7 (issues 07daba29, 48f77301, 436be110; closed 1a5a1a8).\n\n**The lesson: most \"macro\" failures are ordinary compiler gaps in COMPILED haxe.macro code.** A test importing MacroStringTools/Printer fails as COMPILE_FAIL `error[IMPORT]` when those modules don't compile. Chain found under Printer/MacroStringTools:\n- `macro e` in ordinary code (runtime reification) → new `tast/ast_lowering/expr/reify.rs`; objects wrapped `({pos, expr} : haxe.macro.Expr)`.\n- `pkg.Enum.Ctor` value: the qualified split loop RETURNED \"Cannot find type\" at the first failed split — `continue` when the would-be package ends in a Capitalized segment. `pkg.Module.Sub.Ctor(args)` call: the multi-segment call path handled only classes.\n- Local named fn not visible in closures nested in its own body → `lower_named_local_function` (declare = null, then assign; typed up front when fully annotated). Function BODIES had no named-fn statement arm at all (decls/fields.rs).\n- Short calls through function values: pad with null; literals apply defaults on entry via hidden `__opt_a` param (parser-level rewrite, `literal_with_entry_defaults`).\n- `infer_call_type_arguments` handled ONE type variable only; `Lambda.fold\u003cA,B\u003e(Iterable\u003cA\u003e, ..)` → trap stub. Multi-var (ordered by type-param SymbolId), values before function literals, Iterable/Iterator typedef-as-Class vs Array; static_receiver.rs DROPPED HIR type_args; return type substituted from the DECLARED return (computed one had decayed to Dynamic). Skip when an argument is an Anonymous structure (runtime stepper path — TestXML regressed otherwise).\n- Object literal omitting a typedef's optional fields laid out by its own shape outside var/return/assign → `retype_literal_to` (only when it omits an optional field; abstract → underlying; class-registered typedef → resolved alias). MIR `resolve_through_aliases` now follows Class-registered typedefs (E0803 \"ambiguous length\").\n- Macro interpreter: `throw` = MacroError::Thrown(value); typed catch selection; compiler errors bound as `{message,pos,childErrors}`; NeedsTyper caught ONLY by catch-alls (keeps HelperMacros.typeError's documented behaviour, lets typeErrorText defer).\n\n**Traps hit:** zsh does not word-split `$VAR` file lists — `git stash push -- $REST` failed and the following `git stash pop` applied ANOTHER session's stash (test_results.txt conflict). Never chain stash push/pop; verify intermediate commits in the base worktree instead. Haxe 4.3.6 rejects nested-quote interpolation as a call argument.\n\n**Round 2 a5eae7cd (647-\u003e652, issue 015e92b0):** macro-time statics (ClassRegistry static store; ++/--, assignment, in-place array methods, `$v{static}` all route through it); `#if macro` members via `macro_context_view` (re-parse with `macro` defined — the driver's `source` is ALREADY PREPROCESSED, read from disk); memoization was keyed by name+args so `bump()` twice expanded ONCE — now per call site; `@:autoBuild(call)` rewritten to Haxe semantics (transitive, carries the call; the build pass never ran without a plain @:build); interpreter match_pattern gained Array/Object/Extractor/Bind (Expr presents as {expr,pos}); `.match`, comprehensions, Reflect/Type, `sort(Reflect.compare)`.\n\n**Round 3 93927d08 + 4684f295 (652-\u003e653):** `switch e { case W(\"5\"): }` NEVER matched — HirPattern::Literal compared a String by POINTER (now haxe_string_compare; general, not macro-only). Abstracts' macro functions were never scanned/stripped and macro calls inside abstract method bodies never expanded. Parser: `in` binary op (prec 12, right-assoc — tighter than `*`/`%` in Haxe), bare `return` before `)`/`,`, `??=` on any lhs. Instance macros (`a.test()`) need lowering-time dispatch — deliberately NOT done at the syntax level (every test class has `test()`).\n\n**Round 4 e0ad2b3a (653-\u003e658, issue aec78b4):** `macro_system/expr_adt.rs` = THE two-way haxe.macro.Expr mapping (every ExprDef/Constant/Binop/Unop/FunctionKind/ComplexType; case patterns \u003c-\u003e exprs); ast_bridge delegates to it. EMeta names keep the colon (`@:mine` = \":mine\", test_macro_annotation corrected). Bare ctor names in patterns (`OpAdd`, `FArrow`) had bound as CAPTURES. Macro params typed non-Expr get the CONSTANT (`MacroDefinition::bind_argument`; TWO binding paths: expander.rs AND interpreter call_macro_def). `macro a =\u003e b` parses (only there — map literals/extractors read `=\u003e` after a full expression). TRAP: python `str.replace` misses silently — assert every anchor. TRAP: gate.sh is `\u003cNEW\u003e \u003cBASE\u003e`; reversed args overwrote the baseline.\n\n**Round 5 718d8041 (658-\u003e659, issue 71d0c98): haxe.macro.Printer RUNS.** Seven PRE-EXISTING general bugs behind it: (1) `case C(x) if (x\u003e0)` ALWAYS fell through — MIR lowered the guard BEFORE binding (mir/stmt/switch.rs); (2) nested nullary ctor `CString(s, SingleQuotes)` bound as a CAPTURE (matched anything) — resolve against the ctor PARAM's enum (Null\u003cT\u003e unwrap ONLY there: at top level it LOST Issue3061); (3) `this` captured ByMutableRef → lazy cell reused across sibling cases; (4) `This` in a lambda (method value `opt(x, show)`) was never captured → arg SHIFT; (5) recursive inferred String return → `map(method)` Dynamic → join read raw strings as boxes (pre-register syntactic String returns); (6) `eq(String, untypedParam)` specialized String over a BOX; (7) Dynamic Int read as String passed the box as a string (haxe_unbox_if_tag now stringifies scalars). TRAP: casting ANY Dynamic arg to the sibling's type LOST 16 rows (decayed raw scalars unboxed) — restricted to UNANNOTATED PARAMS + String. OPEN 342cb5a: eq(\"lit\", Dynamic expr) rows (10041/11007/9217/8975) gainable once Dynamic `a.toString()` returns its value. TRAP: scratchpad gate.sh/cmp.py/runcase.sh got DELETED mid-session (reports survived) — recreated.\n\n**Round 6 0cc32373 + 55b4d520/9b862300 (659-\u003e666):** Dynamic method dispatch by tag: String's tag was an FNV hash, not TYPE_STRING=5 (String boxes never matched); `toString`/`split`/Array-returning results boxed as tag-0 references (\"void\"). Dynamic STATIC initializers stored unboxed (decl/init.rs). Reflect.callMethod (compile-time lowered, mir/expr/reflect.rs) padded missing args with 0 — now defaults via function_param_defaults + haxe_unbox_erased_return per slot. unify_dynamic_arguments widened to ANY Dynamic but String-only (Int LOST 16). MACRO ORDER: a deferred (typer) macro ran AFTER later syntactic calls → same-class later calls now defer too. Bare-name macro matching crossed modules (`load` in haxe.macro.Context hit a fixture macro) → own methods shadow. `@:const` type args = TypeKind::ConstArgument (only ONE exhaustive match: hash_type_kind); string consts spelled with DOUBLE quotes (single quotes broke HelperMacros.typedAs's parse). HARNESS 9b862300: injected main called `macro function testMacro` — NOT a compiler win. OPEN 4b5a733: nullary ctor == null representation.\n\n**Round 7 e4eefbb9 + d8c88166 (666-\u003e668):** Lambda.has over enums never specialized (monomorphizer infers T only from PRIMITIVE args; TAST withheld type args when T is a direct param, static-extension calls passed NONE) → Printer.printField/printTypeDefinition trap-stubbed. Runtime `macro class` = ExprKind::TypeDecl + reify.rs TypeDefinition builder. `case C([])` nested array pattern was a WILDCARD. TypePath.sub was IGNORED by lower_type. Typedef-of-Array registered as a CLASS when typed before its declaration (`TypeParamDecl.meta : Metadata`) → field reads/receivers retyped late (registered_alias_as_array). Issue8859 #2 needs a Printer NEWER than upstream 4.3.6 (ours is identical; /usr/local/lib/haxe/std is 4.3.6 for diffing). OPEN 91881ac: nested object literal in array literal in typedef literal built untyped. Builds hit 22 min when other sessions (zyntax) compile.\n\n**Round 8 c29856f2 (668-\u003e671):** macro-time ExprTools map/iter/toString; macro_system/printer.rs = case-for-case port of Printer.hx (17/17 byte-identical); `${e}` = `$e{e}`; expr metadata takes a WHOLE expression (`@:m x = 1` = `@:m (x = 1)`, Haxe grammar; moved Issue5039 to the missing @:bypassAccessor); getLocalImports (latest first); Std.string(enum) = `Ctor(a,b)`. kache is OFF (user, 2026-09-25): cold release build ~19 min, incremental ~5-8.\n\n**Round 9 840c8988 + c9eeb5cd/77b712f3 (671-\u003e676):** modules named ONLY in @:build metadata were never loaded (driver.rs build_macro_module_paths); build bodies ran with an EMPTY import map; non-macro static builders; bodyless `macro function f():Expr;` aborted the scan and the file's own macro view was SKIPPED as a dependency (same filename); formatString; Rest.toArray; macro-time `macro class` -\u003e object-form fields. Function-local `static var` reset every call -\u003e parser hoists to a private static field under the local's name (decls.rs hoist_static_locals).\n\n**Still open (next):** Issue6830 needs typedef @:const type args through Context.typeof. Issue3914 crashes re-lowering a stored typed lambda.\n**Older open list:** undefined std globals in the macro interpreter (Type, Reflect, haxe.*), missing Context methods (withImports, getLocalImports, registerFileContents, getTypedExpr), `macro class` reification, Printer.printExpr/printTypeDefinition uncompiled, @:build lookup + scan failures, typeErrorText rows need a stricter typer.\n\nRelated: [[bugs_macro_failure_map_2026_09_06]], [[feature_deferred_typed_macros]], [[bugs_pattern_guard_desugar_and_dynamic_literals]].\n\n---\nArchived from Claude memory `bugs_macro_gaps_runtime_reification_chain` on 2026-10-18. A record of past work; open items in it may have their own issues.","files":null}]}